        "message": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: release and rebuild an HCA on device removal\n\nA VF reset or \"rdma link delete\" with LNet up blocks the device\nunregister in cma_process_remove(). The o2iblnd CM handler ignores\nDEVICE_REMOVAL, and rdma_cm sends no DISCONNECTED after it. So each\nconn keeps its CM ref and its cm_id.\n\nRegister kiblnd_ib_client. Its remove(), kiblnd_hca_remove(), runs\nbefore rdma_cm sends DEVICE_REMOVAL. It makes the NI fatal, closes\nthe conns on the device and drops each CM ref. It returns after the\nlast conn and pool of each hdev on the device are gone. Then\nkiblnd_ib_add() lets the failover thread build a new hdev. That\nthread now always starts, also with dev_failover=0.\n\nkiblnd_cm_device_removal() releases each cm_id that stays, also one\nin address or route resolution. It takes kib_connect_sem to wait\nfor kiblnd_connect_peer(). kiblnd_listen_cm_callback() ignores the\nevent for a listener, because o2iblnd destroys the listener.\n\n    Soft-RoCE, 2 VMs, rdma link delete, then rdma link add\n    without the fix: delete blocked for more than 60 s\n    with the fix:    6 of 6 deletes in 1 s, lctl ping OK after add\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet,sanity\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ib0530e74ba712ad349c2faa7af9dde16b0d06d79\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
